  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Syria: Setting the base to work on inclusion</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Oxfam team in Syria has had a series of conversations in relation to this call, as there is an interest in engaging more with inclusion &#x2013; how to define it, capacity building for staff, improvement of tools and methodologies, and participation of excluded groups in Water Sanitation and Hygiene (WASH)  and Emergency Food Security and Vulnerable Livelihoods (EFSVL) programs &#x2013; as no previous, systematic work has been done in relation to this topic. The conversations have been across programmes as we recognise the importance of improving the understanding of Oxfam in Syria in inclusion of marginalized, vulnerable and people with specific needs, and building capacity across programmes and to all staff members.   As there has not been any comprehensive work on inclusion in the country programmes, the proposal aims to set the base for working more on inclusion by:  1. Increasing the understanding of how communities and historically under -represented groups in Syria define and understand inclusion/exclusion; and 2. Increasing the understanding within the staff members and gain practical tools to work better on inclusion in Oxfam&apos;s programmes.   We propose two areas of work:   1. Definition of inclusion by communities; and   2. Capacity building of Oxfam staff on inclusion  Possible entry points by hubs:  &#x2022; Northern hub (Aleppo, Hama and Lattakia governorates): Currently affected by the earthquake &#x2013; large number of the population has been affected.  Multi -sectoral needs assessment and gender analysis was conducted in March 2023. In addition, Oxfam is a member of Syria Joint Response (SJR) consortium that focuses on supporting the Age, Gender, and Disability (AGD) inclusion in the humanitarian programmes operated by the consortium members in Aleppo. Oxfam and Dorcas are utilizing a SJR top -up fund to lead on an AGD inclusion assessment and analysis to come up with recommendations on how to improve on AGD inclusion within the consortium programme across different locations</narrative>
  </description>
